WEBVTT

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:16.180
MISSION 75
"IT'S JUST WHITE DAY."

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:33.740
H-Here… I-It's friend chocolate.

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:39.080
Tadano replayed Valentine's Day
in his head a hundred times a day.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:40.790
POOF

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:43.790
-MARCH 8
-It's already March.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:46.460
I have to think about White Day gifts.

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:51.460
THE WRAPPER FROM KOMI'S CHOCOLATE

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:55.970
SNIFF

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:58.220
I-It's not what you think!

00:00:58.300 --> 00:00:59.470
Huh? What is?

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:10.440
But what should I give in return?

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:14.240
I hear about candies and marshmallows…

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:20.200
Wow, they have meanings.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:24.660
Candies mean "like."
But marshmallows mean "hate."

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:27.420
Cookies mean "friends."

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:32.210
This just made it worse.

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:37.760
Should I ask Hitomi?

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:41.300
Yeah, but… no…

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:42.930
Yeah, but… no…

00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:44.140
You're distracting!

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:49.150
I was just thinking about
a good return gift for White Day.

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:51.520
White Day?

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:54.690
A return gift for your male friend?

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:55.740
Uh… yeah!

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:56.820
That's it!

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:58.450
What?

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:01.450
If it's a return gift
for chocolate from a boy,

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.330
wouldn't food be alright?

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:05.410
Or you could give chocolate back.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:10.880
I was thinking of something
a little more substantial…

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:12.460
-You're in love?
-WITH THAT BOY

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:14.000
N-No!

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.130
Based on his reaction…

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:18.930
And the shadow on that day…

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:21.930
About 165 centimeters tall,
long-haired silhouette,

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:25.060
and the faint footsteps I heard
were close together!

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:27.140
My brother…

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:29.480
got some chocolate!

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:31.440
W-What's that?

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:34.770
Fine then. I'll help you
think of something.

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:39.070
NO CUSHION FOR ME…

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:41.660
First, was it friend chocolate?

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:43.120
Or real love chocolate?

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:46.830
Um, friend chocolate. I think.

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:47.950
You think?

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:50.080
That's what I was… told.

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.840
It might not be true, though.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:56.500
I guess…

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:58.720
I mean, no!

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.510
I-I don't think that's it.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:07.520
If it's true love chocolate,
a gift that lasts would be nice.

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:09.310
-I see.
-You like this person?

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:11.480
I already said no!

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:13.730
Hang on! Choose between "like" or "hate."

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:16.650
Hm? Oh, in that case…

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:18.150
This is about Katai, right?

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:20.570
"Like" I guess… so what?

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:23.820
-Ugh! That's not what I mean!
-What are you talking about?!

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:24.910
Whoa.

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:28.450
Imagine this person clearly in your head.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:30.200
Listen.

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:32.000
Do you like them?

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:44.340
I suppose… I do have feelings.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:45.260
-Huh?
-SO CUTE.

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:46.430
Why are you mad?

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:49.930
I understand the situation.

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:53.480
To the department store!

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:55.230
H-Hitomi?

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:58.440
I saw it on The Noon Show.

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:00.690
Snacks that look good on social media!

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:02.280
Hitomi!

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:03.610
But listen.

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:06.280
Anything is okay from someone you like!

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:07.530
Don't you think so?

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:12.460
Hitomi!

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:14.960
MOM ONLY KNOWS ABOUT
THE CHOCOLATE FROM A BOY.

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:18.170
March 13, Friday.

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:21.300
White Day falls on a Saturday,
not a school day.

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:24.090
The boys who got chocolate are nervous.

00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:27.720
The girls have already
finished their duties.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.560
They're calm and collected.

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:34.230
The boys who didn't get any chocolate
have reached enlightenment.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:36.690
Komi!

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:38.980
Here's your White Day return gi--

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:41.690
Komi! Here's your White Day return gift!

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:45.150
-CANDY SCULPTURE
-Go on and lick your favorite part of me!

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:54.790
T-Thanks!

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:01.000
-HEART RACING
-Anxiety.

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:03.970
N-Next is the return gift for my mentor!

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:07.220
OMINOUS

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:16.310
-Muscle mass is all I can offer my mentor…
-HOW TO ATTAIN BEAUTIFUL MUSCLES

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:20.270
D-Does she like it?

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:23.320
And then there's Tadano.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:24.900
Oh yeah!

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:28.820
Want to eat something
after school today? My treat.

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:30.780
-Katai.
-BEEF BOWL?

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:32.330
He faltered!

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:36.660
A result of being
too nervous to give Komi her gift.

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:40.000
He told himself,
"T-Today's an unlucky day."

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:41.880
In the end he couldn't do it.

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:45.130
Huh? A date?

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:47.590
That's a date, isn't it?!

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:52.180
And so Friday the 13th
passed uneventfully.

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:54.930
-MARCH 14, SATURDAY
-White Day.

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:57.480
While everyone else was giving out gifts,

00:05:57.560 --> 00:05:59.810
Tadano had faltered.

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:03.780
Now he had no other choice
but to go to Komi's and hand it over.

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:09.280
-Don't stay out too late!
-SMIRK

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:12.580
See ya.

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:22.590
I never thought I'd be this nervous.

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:25.050
I came to her house.

00:06:25.130 --> 00:06:28.170
I… I hope she doesn't
take it the wrong way.

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:31.640
No, I'll just hand it over at the door.

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:33.300
It'll be fine…

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:34.390
It might not be fine.

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:35.640
-Suspicious?
-UNSTABLE

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:38.390
But…

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:41.650
I guess she was…

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:44.070
even more nervous than this.

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:46.110
KOMI

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:58.120
-TADANO IS FALTERING
-I pushed it! I want to run away!

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:01.710
Yes?

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:03.380
S-Someone answered!

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:06.340
-MALE VOICE… HER YOUNGER BROTHER?
-Um, is Komi…

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:10.050
Uh, is S-Shoko there?

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:12.260
I-I'm a friend from school.

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:14.510
I-It's uh, Tadano.

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:19.560
-BEEP
-He hung up?!

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:24.900
-W-What's wrong, Tadano?
-MOTHER

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:28.440
-Hello. Is Shoko home?
-TADANO RESPONDED NORMALLY.

00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:31.530
Shoko is out on an errand.

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:34.160
Sorry for the bad timing.

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:36.490
Oh, uh, I'll come back later…

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:38.450
Come in and wait!

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:42.670
-Come in and wait!
-Uh… Um…

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:48.630
I'll bring some tea.
Make yourself at home.

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:51.800
Oh, thanks. Don't mind me.

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:01.640
-What should I do?
-SQUIRM

00:08:02.230 --> 00:08:03.730
Oh, sor…

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:07.150
Her father?

00:08:13.490 --> 00:08:15.820
T-Thank you.

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:17.950
-SITTING
-He's sitting?!

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:23.620
W-What?

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:27.290
-SIP
-Oh, he's drinking it.

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:31.960
-COULDN'T HANDLE THE SILENCE
-M-My name is Hitohito Tadano.

00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:34.010
I'm Ko… ah, Sho…

00:08:34.090 --> 00:08:37.550
I'm in your daughter's class,
and I study hard every day!

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:39.260
And, uh.

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:42.730
She gave me some friend chocolate
for Valentine's Day.

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:44.730
So I came to give a return gi…

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:46.730
Sir!

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:50.360
BANG

00:08:53.650 --> 00:08:55.320
PUSH

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:56.570
TADANO IS FLUSTERED

00:08:59.910 --> 00:09:03.580
OPEN CLOSET, SCATTERED BOOKS
CAST-OFF CLOTHES, MESSY BLANKET

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:08.330
-BAM BOOM SLAM CRUNCH
-I-It's not that messy!

00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:12.840
WHEW

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:14.970
SLOWS HER BREATH

00:09:15.050 --> 00:09:17.340
TADANO WATCHES AND WAITS

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:18.590
KOMI CALMS DOWN

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:21.600
ADJUSTS HIS POSTURE

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:22.970
HASN'T CALMED DOWN

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:26.560
TADANO DRINKS DAD'S TEA

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:31.020
TADANO CAN'T FIND A WAY TO START

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:34.280
KOMI KNOWS TODAY IS WHITE DAY.

00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:40.740
Uh.

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:43.370
Oh. No. Sorry.

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:49.210
This is, uh, thank you
for the Valentines' gift.

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:51.750
H-Here's the return gift.

00:09:59.890 --> 00:10:02.180
Go ahead. Look inside.

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:04.180
HAND CREAM

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:05.640
CUTE!

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:08.440
It's not quite the right season anymore.

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:12.190
But I found one
with a nice smell, so I chose it.

00:10:13.150 --> 00:10:15.740
-I hope you like it.
-BOW

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:28.910
That's uh… a candy.

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:43.010
W-Well, I'll get going!

00:10:43.970 --> 00:10:46.930
I don't want to disturb your day off.

00:10:47.020 --> 00:10:48.230
Can't have that!

00:10:48.310 --> 00:10:49.600
NOD

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:16.920
IT SMELLED GOOD.

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:20.300
-Sato, hold this!
-Sure!

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:23.300
Komi.

00:11:23.390 --> 00:11:26.680
Is this rag alright for wiping desks?

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:33.560
Komi?

00:11:33.650 --> 00:11:35.480
Die!

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:37.860
ROLL

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:43.450
-Let's play Eraser Drop!
-ERASER DROP

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:44.370
Huh? Why?

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:46.030
Eraser Drop.

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:47.240
The history of humanity.

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:51.790
All its wisdom was concentrated
in creating this object, the eraser.

00:11:51.870 --> 00:11:55.670
-By the hand of man, it was created…
-The last eraser on the desk wins!

00:11:55.750 --> 00:11:57.920
-My time to shine.
-YADANO, 10 YEARS

00:11:58.000 --> 00:11:59.550
The battlefield for the tournament is…

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:00.920
Tadano's desk.

00:12:01.010 --> 00:12:01.920
Set!

00:12:02.010 --> 00:12:02.840
Round one.

00:12:02.930 --> 00:12:04.430
SPEED STAR NZ3, MAKERU ERASER,
KOMI'S ERASER, ZAFU II

00:12:04.510 --> 00:12:06.220
-Fight!
-BEAM

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:08.180
First and best!

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:09.180
-Whoa!
-GRIND

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:12.180
She's sticking her eraser down
with kneaded eraser!

00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:14.400
-It's the "Barricade!"
-GRIND

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:16.770
BARRICADE:
STICKING THE ERASER TO THE DESK.

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:21.780
Komi, you can go first.

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:25.200
PLINK

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:26.570
Ox walk.

00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:29.200
-Komi's biding her time?
-OX WALK - BARELY MOVING THE ERASER

00:12:29.290 --> 00:12:32.080
-She's using a good strategy!
-SHE JUST MISSED IT

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:34.580
WHO ARE YOU TALKING TO?

00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:36.330
Alright, my turn.

00:12:36.420 --> 00:12:39.300
Die!

00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:46.890
NAJIMI OSANA DISQUALIFIED

00:12:46.970 --> 00:12:48.470
I'm up next.

00:12:48.550 --> 00:12:50.430
UNGH!

00:12:50.510 --> 00:12:53.230
She ruined her barricade setup
and sent it flying!

00:12:53.310 --> 00:12:54.980
Why?!

00:12:55.060 --> 00:12:59.270
OUT OF BOUNDS
YADANO MAKERU DISQUALIFIED

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:01.070
Next is Tadano.

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:09.370
-ZAFU II
-KOMI'S ERASER

00:13:09.450 --> 00:13:11.790
WAH!

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:17.170
WHOOSH!

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:18.330
THUNK

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:22.210
-Hitohito Tadano, disqualified.
-EXCITED

00:13:22.300 --> 00:13:24.130
Komi wins by elimination.

00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:25.880
Alright, next game!

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:27.340
The time has come.

00:13:27.430 --> 00:13:30.220
-I know you want to see my power.
-NAKANAKA 4 YEARS EXPERIENCE

00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:33.520
New challenger, Nakanaka!

00:13:33.600 --> 00:13:36.100
-Don't worry, Komi!
-You!

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:37.900
New challenger, Yamai.

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:41.730
I'd die to sacrifice my life
for Komi's eraser.

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:44.860
That's like saying your headache hurts.

00:13:44.940 --> 00:13:46.030
-Huh?
-Ah?

00:13:46.110 --> 00:13:49.490
The phoenix Najimi rises again!

00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:51.120
Round two.

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:52.120
Fight!

00:13:54.450 --> 00:13:56.040
Oh my.

00:13:56.120 --> 00:13:57.120
What's this?

00:13:57.210 --> 00:13:59.460
Eraser Drop! I want to play too!

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:03.380
Huh? Wasn't this
a turn battle type of game?

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:05.380
Me too!

00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:07.420
We're reserving the third match.

00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:08.380
12 YEARS, 7 YEARS, 5 YEARS

00:14:08.470 --> 00:14:11.350
Everyone's too excited
to play Eraser Drop!

00:14:11.430 --> 00:14:15.100
This will be a fierce battle
to end all Eraser Drop battles!

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:18.770
It has already blown away
the concept of a turn battle!

00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:20.020
Is that allowed?

00:14:20.100 --> 00:14:20.940
Okay!

00:14:21.020 --> 00:14:24.110
Third battle for the second round
at this desk!

00:14:24.190 --> 00:14:25.860
Consolation match over here!

00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:26.780
A tournament?

00:14:26.860 --> 00:14:29.280
I don't know how I wound up playing.

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:30.780
What should I do?!

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:33.530
I've never played Eraser Drop before!

00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:35.040
And why the crowd?

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:39.540
NOD

00:14:40.960 --> 00:14:44.040
I'll show you a real eraser battle.

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:55.890
It's okay.

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:58.180
Hey! That stage!

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:02.350
Nakanaka is tired!

00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:04.110
She exhausted her finger!

00:15:04.190 --> 00:15:05.610
Weak constitution!

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:07.480
What's that?

00:15:08.990 --> 00:15:11.240
Using a finger reinforcement device!

00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:13.740
That's cheating! You're a cheater, Najimi!

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:16.740
Winning is all that matters!

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:20.290
Now! Komi's…

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:32.010
FLICK

00:15:40.350 --> 00:15:43.270
…single shot!

00:15:43.350 --> 00:15:45.520
WOOO!

00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:52.530
-Right here…
-Yeah! You can do it!

00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:53.610
-Wow!
-Yes.

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:54.530
I knew it.

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:57.530
Uh, ah, i-is it my turn?

00:15:57.620 --> 00:16:00.040
That was not okay.

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:02.290
What should I do?

00:16:04.120 --> 00:16:05.330
Yay!

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:09.420
Yay! Third battle!

00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:11.420
Don't worry about it!

00:16:11.510 --> 00:16:13.680
It's a comeback!

00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:15.550
-I'm next!
-No, me!

00:16:15.640 --> 00:16:17.760
-Me!
-It is I!

00:16:17.850 --> 00:16:19.680
Oh, right. Komi,
you've got a second ma…

00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:25.810
Komi?

00:16:28.020 --> 00:16:32.490
Are you alright? Do you feel sick?

00:16:33.740 --> 00:16:35.860
SORRY. IT'S OKAY. I'M FINE.

00:16:35.950 --> 00:16:37.160
I see.

00:16:45.170 --> 00:16:46.170
Hey, Tadano.

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:48.670
-I have something to do! Bye!
-WHAT ABOUT STUDENT COUNCIL?

00:16:48.750 --> 00:16:50.170
Hey!

00:16:52.260 --> 00:16:55.880
My ally. Let us meet in battle
another day.

00:16:55.970 --> 00:16:59.390
G-Good work again today!

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:01.390
-Bye-bye Komi!
-Kiss me goodbye!

00:17:01.470 --> 00:17:02.350
WHACK

00:17:02.430 --> 00:17:05.850
-Bye! Take care!
-TODAY I WILL GREET KOMI.

00:17:36.590 --> 00:17:38.840
It's raining, huh.

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:41.310
Do you have an umbrella?

00:17:41.970 --> 00:17:44.220
I HAVE A FOLDING UMBRELLA.

00:17:44.310 --> 00:17:45.520
Oh, good.

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:47.640
I brought one too.

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:08.870
I'm… sad.

00:18:13.170 --> 00:18:16.220
There are only a few days…

00:18:17.170 --> 00:18:19.430
until the end of year assembly.

00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:24.720
A little… over a week.

00:18:25.640 --> 00:18:28.940
A-And we'll start with new classes.

00:18:30.850 --> 00:18:33.650
This time will end.

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:36.780
And I'm sad.

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:43.030
I understand.

00:18:50.710 --> 00:18:54.290
This year has gone by so fast.

00:19:03.680 --> 00:19:05.680
At first, you made friends with Najimi.

00:19:06.270 --> 00:19:08.140
Najimi says some pretty wild things,

00:19:08.230 --> 00:19:12.060
but thanks to them, everyone got closer.

00:19:12.150 --> 00:19:14.480
They're pretty relentless.

00:19:16.730 --> 00:19:20.280
And then you made friends with Agari.

00:19:20.360 --> 00:19:23.620
Agari really surprised us
when we went to eat with her.

00:19:24.410 --> 00:19:26.910
We should go out to eat together again.

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:33.500
Yamai and Nakanaka are like cats and dogs,

00:19:33.580 --> 00:19:36.460
but I think they make a good pair.

00:19:40.090 --> 00:19:45.010
Onemine and Otori are both so reliable.

00:19:45.100 --> 00:19:46.930
They feel so safe.

00:19:47.560 --> 00:19:49.390
Like they can take care of things.

00:19:51.890 --> 00:19:53.270
On the field trip,

00:19:53.350 --> 00:19:56.770
you got to know Kato and Sasaki.

00:19:59.230 --> 00:20:01.860
I was glad about that, too.

00:20:04.410 --> 00:20:06.280
Sato's morning cleaning.

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:09.620
It's too bad we could only
help towards the end.

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:15.330
She's been doing it all along
and I feel guilty.

00:20:17.790 --> 00:20:21.510
It would be nice to hang out
with Maeda and Ushiroda, too.

00:20:25.010 --> 00:20:26.930
Sports Day, the Culture Festival…

00:20:27.010 --> 00:20:29.180
going shopping, going to the pool.

00:20:29.260 --> 00:20:31.180
Going to the festival…

00:20:31.270 --> 00:20:36.020
the Christmas party, the snowball fight,
visiting the shrine, and buying fortunes.

00:20:53.710 --> 00:20:56.420
The rain isn't stopping.

00:20:58.750 --> 00:21:02.380
But it will stop sometime.

00:21:09.550 --> 00:21:11.930
It's like…

00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:16.020
comparing the rainstorm
while trying to say something profound…

00:21:16.100 --> 00:21:18.810
but it was harder than I thought.

00:21:21.860 --> 00:21:23.650
Silly me.

00:21:26.910 --> 00:21:28.450
Silly you.

00:21:31.490 --> 00:21:33.540
-BANG!
-I forgot my eraser!

00:21:33.620 --> 00:21:34.450
THUMP

00:21:34.540 --> 00:21:36.960
Huh? You two haven't left yet?

00:21:37.040 --> 00:21:39.460
Let's go together!
Let me in your umbrella.

00:21:39.540 --> 00:21:41.880
Didn't you have something to do?

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:42.880
HM?

00:21:42.960 --> 00:21:45.010
-Don't give me that.
-YOU JUST WANTED TO LEAVE EARLY…

00:21:46.510 --> 00:21:50.260
Do you want to invite everyone out
after the last day of school?

00:21:50.350 --> 00:21:51.310
Yeah!

00:21:51.390 --> 00:21:54.220
Okay, Komi. You invite everyone!

00:21:56.520 --> 00:21:57.520
NOD

00:21:57.600 --> 00:22:00.770
D-Don't push yourself too hard!

00:22:13.990 --> 00:22:15.410
NOD

00:22:15.500 --> 00:22:17.460
NUMBER 6
FEBRUARY TO MARCH

00:22:17.540 --> 00:22:18.960
NUMBER 7
APRIL

00:22:54.530 --> 00:22:55.870
SECOND YEAR STUDENTS

00:23:05.670 --> 00:23:06.630
KOMI

00:23:15.600 --> 00:23:17.890
Good morning, Komi.

00:23:20.060 --> 00:23:23.190
GOOD MORNING

00:23:36.490 --> 00:23:37.410
I…

00:23:37.910 --> 00:23:40.500
I hope we…

00:23:41.790 --> 00:23:47.460
can… have another…

00:23:52.720 --> 00:23:53.970
good year.

00:23:54.050 --> 00:23:55.260
WHEN A PERSON HAS EXTREME SOCIAL ANXIETY,
THEY STRUGGLE TO COMMUNICATE WITH OTHERS.

00:23:55.350 --> 00:23:56.600
BEAR IN MIND,
THEY ONLY STRUGGLE TO FORM CONNECTIONS.

00:23:56.680 --> 00:23:57.970
IT DOESN'T MEAN THEY DON'T WANT TO.

00:23:58.060 --> 00:24:01.020
Subtitle translation by: Claire Tanaka
